          "text": "Reported upper respiratory symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Five days of sneezing, blocked nose, clear rhinorrhoea, and mild frontal heaviness. No significant fevers at home. Mild sore throat early in the illness, now resolved. Minimal dry cough. Denies shortness of breath, chest pain, wheeze, ear pain, facial swelling, tooth pain, and purulent discharge. Sleep slightly reduced due to congestion."
      }
